\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces RL bridge dataflow. The \texttt  {lane\_reference\_node}, the LiDAR-based \texttt  {hitch\_angle\_estimator}, and Autoware localization supply the policy observation to \texttt  {rl\_bridge\_node}, which queries the TD3 policy at 10\,Hz and emits a control command that \texttt  {controller\_canbridge} translates into Hunter SE CAN frames. Vehicle velocity and steering feedback return through the same bridge.\relax }}{67}{figure.caption.70}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rl_bridge}{{5.3}{67}{RL bridge dataflow. The \texttt {lane\_reference\_node}, the LiDAR-based \texttt {hitch\_angle\_estimator}, and Autoware localization supply the policy observation to \texttt {rl\_bridge\_node}, which queries the TD3 policy at 10\,Hz and emits a control command that \texttt {controller\_canbridge} translates into Hunter SE CAN frames. Vehicle velocity and steering feedback return through the same bridge.\relax }{figure.caption.70}{}}
\newlabel{fig:rl_bridge@cref}{{[figure][3][5]5.3}{[1][66][]67}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The deployment running in RViz. The left panel shows the occupancy image the policy consumes, drivable in white and blocked in black, built from the lanelet map and the infrastructure obstacle list. The right panel shows the same scene in the map frame, with the tractor and trailer, the LiDAR return field, and the estimated hitch angle annotated on the vehicle.\relax }}{67}{figure.caption.71}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rviz_deployment}{{5.4}{67}{The deployment running in RViz. The left panel shows the occupancy image the policy consumes, drivable in white and blocked in black, built from the lanelet map and the infrastructure obstacle list. The right panel shows the same scene in the map frame, with the tractor and trailer, the LiDAR return field, and the estimated hitch angle annotated on the vehicle.\relax }{figure.caption.71}{}}
